IMPORT `ssc-core`

-- Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992 (United Kingdom), 1992 c. 4.
-- SCHEDULE 1, paragraphs 6 to 11: supplementary provisions relating to contributions of Classes 1, 1A, 1B, 2, 3 and 3A
-- (ssc8, layer 1, second half: interest, penalties, collection, deduction from a pension, sickness payments).
-- Source: ukpga-1992-4.txt, a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from legislation.gov.uk
-- (point in time 2026-07-08). It is not the official text and nothing here is "verified against the official text".
--
-- Paragraph numbers: the rendering drops them. The Act and the Schedule cite 6 ("paragraph 6 above", src:4605, 4683), 7 (4587, 4641),
-- 7B (4686, 4688) and 8 (src:1881). Paragraphs 7A (src:4641), 7C (4686), 7D (4689), 7E (4690), 9 (4737), 10 (4741) and 11 (4744) are
-- labelled BY INFERENCE FROM THEIR POSITION: see NOTES.md. Paragraphs 4, 5, 5A, 6(1)-(2), 7B(1)-(2), 7C(1)-(2), 7D, 7E, 8 and 9 and the
-- regulation-making parts of 7, 7A, 7B and 11 are powers to make regulations; they are listed in the coverage table as machinery
-- and encoded nowhere, except for the limits the Act itself puts on what the regulations may require.
--
-- INPUTS: the rates of interest (prescribed under section 178 of the Finance Act 1989), the maximum penalties under section 98A of the
-- Taxes Management Act 1970, the dates, and every "regulations so provide" are facts the person (or the lead at the merge) states.
-- Amounts are in pounds.

§ `Schedule 1 -- paragraphs 6 to 11`

§§ `Paragraph 6 -- power to combine collection of contributions with tax`

DECLARE `sch 1 para 6(2) kind of thing referred to` IS ONE OF
    `sch 1 para 6(2) interest in respect of contributions or income tax`
    `sch 1 para 6(2) a penalty in respect of contributions or income tax`
    `sch 1 para 6(2) something else`

-- (2), end: "any reference to contributions or income tax in paragraph (b) or (c) of sub-paragraph (1) above shall be construed as including a reference to any interest or penalty in
-- respect of contributions or income tax, as the case may be".
-- src:4588 | and any reference to contributions or income tax in paragraph (b) or (c) of sub-paragraph (1) above shall be construed as including a reference to any interest or penalty in respect of contributions or income tax, as the case may be.
@ref sch 1 para 6(2) (src:4588)
GIVEN thing IS A `sch 1 para 6(2) kind of thing referred to`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 6(2) the reference in sub-paragraph (1)(b) or (c) includes the thing` MEANS
    CONSIDER thing
    WHEN `sch 1 para 6(2) interest in respect of contributions or income tax` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 1 para 6(2) a penalty in respect of contributions or income tax` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "construed as including" does not close the list
    WHEN `sch 1 para 6(2) something else` THEN NOTHING

-- (3): "The rate of interest applicable for any purpose of this paragraph shall be the rate from time to time prescribed for that purpose under section 178 of the Finance Act 1989."
-- src:4589 | (3) The rate of interest applicable for any purpose of this paragraph shall be the rate from time to time prescribed for that purpose under section 178 of the Finance Act 1989.
@ref sch 1 para 6(3) (src:4589)
GIVEN `the rate from time to time prescribed for the purpose under section 178 of the Finance Act 1989` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`sch 1 para 6(3) the rate of interest` MEANS
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the prescribed rate is not in this text and is an input
    `the rate from time to time prescribed for the purpose under section 178 of the Finance Act 1989`

-- (4): where a decision relating to contributions falls to be made under or by virtue of section 8, 10 or 11 of the 1999 Act and will affect liability for, or the amount of, any
-- interest due, "regulations under sub-paragraph (1) above shall not require any such interest to be paid until the decision has been made".
-- src:4590 | (4) Where—
-- src:4591 | (a) a decision relating to contributions falls to be made under or by virtue of section 8, 10 or 11 of the Social Security Contributions (Transfer of Functions, etc.) Act 1999; and
-- src:4592 | (b) the decision will affect a person’s liability for, or the amount of, any interest due in respect of those contributions,
-- src:4593 | regulations under sub-paragraph (1) above shall not require any such interest to be paid until the decision has been made.
@ref sch 1 para 6(4) (src:4590-4593)
GIVEN `a decision relating to contributions falls to be made under or by virtue of section 8, 10 or 11 of the Social Security Contributions (Transfer of Functions, etc.) Act 1999` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision will affect a person's liability for, or the amount of, any interest due in respect of those contributions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision has been made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 6(4) regulations under sub-paragraph (1) may require the interest to be paid` MEANS
    IF `a decision relating to contributions falls to be made under or by virtue of section 8, 10 or 11 of the Social Security Contributions (Transfer of Functions, etc.) Act 1999`
       AND `the decision will affect a person's liability for, or the amount of, any interest due in respect of those contributions`
       AND (NOT `the decision has been made`)
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "regulations under sub-paragraph (1) above shall not require any such interest to be paid until the decision has been made"
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar lasts "until the decision has been made" and covers only the cases described; the sub-paragraph grants nothing
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (4A): "Regulations under sub-paragraph (1) above shall not require the payment of interest on a sum due in respect of a Class 1B contribution if a relevant tax appeal has been brought but not finally determined".
-- src:4594 | (4A) Regulations under sub-paragraph (1) above shall not require the payment of interest on a sum due in respect of a Class 1B contribution if a relevant tax appeal has been brought but not finally determined; and “a relevant tax appeal” means an appeal against a determination as to the amount of income tax in respect of which the person liable to pay the Class 1B contribution is accountable in accordance with the relevant PAYE settlement agreement.
@ref sch 1 para 6(4A) (src:4594)
GIVEN `the appeal is against a determination as to the amount of income tax in respect of which the person liable to pay the Class 1B contribution is accountable in accordance with the relevant PAYE settlement agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appeal has been brought` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appeal has been finally determined` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 6(4A) regulations under sub-paragraph (1) may require interest on the Class 1B sum to be paid` MEANS
    IF `the appeal is against a determination as to the amount of income tax in respect of which the person liable to pay the Class 1B contribution is accountable in accordance with the relevant PAYE settlement agreement`
       AND `the appeal has been brought`
       AND (NOT `the appeal has been finally determined`)
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall not require the payment of interest on a sum due in respect of a Class 1B contribution if a relevant tax appeal has been brought but not finally determined"
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar is for a "relevant tax appeal" "brought but not finally determined"; otherwise the sub-paragraph says nothing
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (4B): interest required to be paid by virtue of (2)(a) or (b) "shall be paid without any deduction of income tax and shall not be taken into account in computing any income, profits or losses for any tax purposes".
-- src:4595 | (4B) Interest required to be paid, by virtue of sub-paragraph (2)(a) or (b) above, by regulations under sub-paragraph (1) above shall be paid without any deduction of income tax and shall not be taken into account in computing any income, profits or losses for any tax purposes.
@ref sch 1 para 6(4B) (src:4595)
GIVEN `the interest is required to be paid by virtue of sub-paragraph (2)(a) or (b) by regulations under sub-paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 6(4B) a deduction of income tax is made from the interest` MEANS
    IF `the interest is required to be paid by virtue of sub-paragraph (2)(a) or (b) by regulations under sub-paragraph (1)`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be paid without any deduction of income tax"
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Interest required to be paid, by virtue of sub-paragraph (2)(a) or (b) above, by regulations under sub-paragraph (1) above"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:4595 | (4B) Interest required to be paid, by virtue of sub-paragraph (2)(a) or (b) above, by regulations under sub-paragraph (1) above shall be paid without any deduction of income tax and shall not be taken into account in computing any income, profits or losses for any tax purposes.
@ref sch 1 para 6(4B) (src:4595)
GIVEN `the interest is required to be paid by virtue of sub-paragraph (2)(a) or (b) by regulations under sub-paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 6(4B) the interest is taken into account in computing income, profits or losses for tax purposes` MEANS
    IF `the interest is required to be paid by virtue of sub-paragraph (2)(a) or (b) by regulations under sub-paragraph (1)`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall not be taken into account in computing any income, profits or losses for any tax purposes"
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Interest required to be paid, by virtue of sub-paragraph (2)(a) or (b) above, by regulations under sub-paragraph (1) above"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (4C): interest under section 101 of the Finance Act 2009 on sums due in respect of Class 1 contributions "is not to be taken into account in computing any income, profits or losses for any tax purposes".
-- src:4596 | (4C) Interest payable under section 101 of the Finance Act 2009 (late payment interest on sums due to HMRC) on sums due in respect of Class 1 contributions is not to be taken into account in computing any income, profits or losses for any tax purposes.
@ref sch 1 para 6(4C) (src:4596)
GIVEN `the interest is payable under section 101 of the Finance Act 2009 on sums due in respect of Class 1 contributions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 6(4C) the interest is taken into account in computing income, profits or losses for tax purposes` MEANS
    IF `the interest is payable under section 101 of the Finance Act 2009 on sums due in respect of Class 1 contributions`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is not to be taken into account in computing any income, profits or losses for any tax purposes"
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sub-paragraph is about interest under section 101 on sums due in respect of Class 1 contributions
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Paragraph 7 -- special penalties in the case of certain returns`

-- (1): this paragraph applies where regulations under paragraph 6(1) require a contributions return to be made (a) at the same time as a specified tax return, or (b) if that tax return does not fall to be
-- made, at a time defined by reference to the time for making it had it fallen to be made.
-- src:4605 | (1) This paragraph applies where regulations under sub-paragraph (1) of paragraph 6 above make provision requiring any return which is to be made in accordance with a specified provision of regulations under that sub-paragraph (the “contributions return”) to be made—
-- src:4606 | (a) at the same time as any specified return required to be made in accordance with a provision of PAYE regulations or regulations made under section 70(1)(a) or 71 (sub-contractors) of the Finance Act 2004 to which section 98A of the Taxes Management Act 1970 applies (the “tax return”); or
-- src:4607 | (b) if the circumstances are such that the return mentioned in paragraph (a) above does not fall to be made, at a time defined by reference to the time for making that return, had it fallen to be made;
-- src:4608 | and, in a case falling within paragraph (b) above, any reference in the following provisions of this paragraph to the tax return shall be construed as a reference to the return there mentioned.
@ref sch 1 para 7(1) (src:4605-4608)
GIVEN `regulations under paragraph 6(1) require the contributions return to be made at the same time as a specified tax return` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the tax return does not fall to be made and the regulations define the time for the contributions return by reference to the time for making the tax return had it fallen to be made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 7(1) this paragraph applies` MEANS
    IF `regulations under paragraph 6(1) require the contributions return to be made at the same time as a specified tax return`
       OR `the tax return does not fall to be made and the regulations define the time for the contributions return by reference to the time for making the tax return had it fallen to be made`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This paragraph applies where" regulations make a provision of the two kinds
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (2): where this paragraph applies and the regulations so provide, section 98A applies to the contributions return as it applies to the tax return, and sections 100 to 100D and 102 to 105 apply to a penalty under it.
-- src:4609 | (2) Where this paragraph applies, regulations under paragraph 6(1) above may provide that section 98A of the Taxes Management Act 1970 (penalties for late, fraudulent or negligent returns) shall apply in relation to any specified provision of regulations in accordance with which the contributions return is required to be made; and where they so provide then, subject to the following provisions of this paragraph—
-- src:4610 | (a) that section shall apply in relation to the contributions return as it applies in relation to the tax return; and
-- src:4611 | (b) sections 100 to 100D and 102 to 105 of that Act shall apply in relation to a penalty under section 98A of that Act to which a person is liable by virtue of this sub-paragraph as they apply in relation to any other penalty under that section.
@ref sch 1 para 7(2) (src:4609-4611)
GIVEN `this paragraph applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `regulations under paragraph 6(1) provide that section 98A of the Taxes Management Act 1970 applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 7(2) section 98A of the Taxes Management Act 1970 applies to the contributions return as to the tax return` MEANS
    IF `this paragraph applies` EQUALS JUST TRUE
       AND `regulations under paragraph 6(1) provide that section 98A of the Taxes Management Act 1970 applies`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where this paragraph applies, regulations ... may provide ...; and where they so provide"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (3): a person required to pay a penalty under section 98A(2)(a) in consequence of a failure in respect of a tax return "shall not also be required to pay a penalty under that paragraph in respect of any failure in respect of the associated contributions return".
-- src:4612 | (3) Where a person has been required to pay a penalty under paragraph (a) of subsection (2) of section 98A of that Act (first twelve months’ default) in consequence of a failure in respect of a tax return, he shall not also be required to pay a penalty under that paragraph in respect of any failure in respect of the associated contributions return.
@ref sch 1 para 7(3) (src:4612)
GIVEN `the person has been required to pay a penalty under paragraph (a) of subsection (2) of section 98A in consequence of a failure in respect of a tax return` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 7(3) the person may also be required to pay a penalty under paragraph (a) for the associated contributions return` MEANS
    IF `the person has been required to pay a penalty under paragraph (a) of subsection (2) of section 98A in consequence of a failure in respect of a tax return`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "he shall not also be required to pay a penalty under that paragraph in respect of any failure in respect of the associated contributions return"
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where a person has been required to pay a penalty under paragraph (a) of subsection (2) of section 98A of that Act"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (5): the limit is the sum of the maximum penalty for the tax return only and the maximum for the associated contributions return only.
-- src:4617 | (5) The limit mentioned in sub-paragraph (4) above is an amount equal to the sum of—
-- src:4618 | (a) the maximum penalty that would have been applicable under subsection (2)(b) or (4) of section 98A of that Act (as the case may be) for a penalty in relation to the tax return only; and
-- src:4619 | (b) the maximum penalty that would have been so applicable in relation to the associated contributions return only.
@ref sch 1 para 7(5) (src:4617-4619)
GIVEN `the maximum penalty that would have been applicable for the tax return only` IS A NUMBER
      `the maximum penalty that would have been applicable for the associated contributions return only` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`sch 1 para 7(5) the limit of the single penalty` MEANS
    `the maximum penalty that would have been applicable for the tax return only`
        PLUS `the maximum penalty that would have been applicable for the associated contributions return only`

-- (4): where a person is liable to a penalty under section 98A(2)(b) or (4) in respect of both returns and an authorised officer has determined to impose a penalty in respect of both, "the penalty so imposed shall be
-- a single penalty of an amount not exceeding the limit".
-- src:4613 | (4) In any case where—
-- src:4614 | (a) a person is liable to a penalty under subsection (2)(b) or (4) of that section (tax-related penalties) in respect of both a tax return and its associated contributions return, and
-- src:4615 | (b) an officer of the Inland Revenue authorised for the purposes of section 100 of that Act has determined that a penalty is to be imposed under that provision in respect of both returns,
-- src:4616 | the penalty so imposed shall be a single penalty of an amount not exceeding the limit determined under sub-paragraph (5) below.
@ref sch 1 para 7(4) (src:4613-4616)
GIVEN `the person is liable to a penalty under subsection (2)(b) or (4) of section 98A in respect of both a tax return and its associated contributions return` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an authorised officer has determined that a penalty is to be imposed in respect of both returns` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the penalty the officer proposes` IS A NUMBER
      limit IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`sch 1 para 7(4) the single penalty that may be imposed` MEANS
    IF `the person is liable to a penalty under subsection (2)(b) or (4) of section 98A in respect of both a tax return and its associated contributions return`
       AND `an authorised officer has determined that a penalty is to be imposed in respect of both returns`
    THEN JUST (min `the penalty the officer proposes` limit)
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In any case where" the person is liable in respect of both returns and an officer has so determined
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (6): the part of a single penalty recovered, after deduction of the administrative costs, is apportioned between income tax and contributions in the ratio T:C, where T and C are the maximum penalties for the tax return only
-- and for the associated contributions return only.
-- src:4620 | (6) So much of any single penalty imposed by virtue of sub-paragraph (4) above as is recovered by the Inland Revenue shall, after the deduction of any administrative costs of the Inland Revenue attributable to its recovery, for the purposes of making any payment into the National Insurance Fund be apportioned between income tax and contributions in the ratio T:C, where—
-- src:4621 | T is the maximum penalty that could have been imposed under the provision in question in relation to the tax return only; and
-- src:4622 | C is the maximum penalty that could have been so imposed in relation to the associated contributions return only.
@ref sch 1 para 7(6) (src:4620-4622)
GIVEN `the amount recovered after the deduction of administrative costs` IS A NUMBER
      T IS A NUMBER
      C IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`sch 1 para 7(6) the part apportioned to income tax` MEANS
    IF (T PLUS C) GREATER THAN 0
    THEN JUST (`the amount recovered after the deduction of administrative costs` TIMES T DIVIDED BY (T PLUS C))
    -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): a ratio T:C of two nils is not defined
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:4620 | (6) So much of any single penalty imposed by virtue of sub-paragraph (4) above as is recovered by the Inland Revenue shall, after the deduction of any administrative costs of the Inland Revenue attributable to its recovery, for the purposes of making any payment into the National Insurance Fund be apportioned between income tax and contributions in the ratio T:C, where—
-- src:4621 | T is the maximum penalty that could have been imposed under the provision in question in relation to the tax return only; and
-- src:4622 | C is the maximum penalty that could have been so imposed in relation to the associated contributions return only.
@ref sch 1 para 7(6) (src:4620-4622)
GIVEN `the amount recovered after the deduction of administrative costs` IS A NUMBER
      T IS A NUMBER
      C IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`sch 1 para 7(6) the part apportioned to contributions` MEANS
    IF (T PLUS C) GREATER THAN 0
    THEN JUST (`the amount recovered after the deduction of administrative costs` TIMES C DIVIDED BY (T PLUS C))
    -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): a ratio T:C of two nils is not defined
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (8): sub-paragraph (6) "shall have effect notwithstanding any provision which treats a penalty under section 98A of that Act as if it were tax charged in an assessment and due and payable".
-- src:4624 | (8) Sub-paragraph (6) above shall have effect notwithstanding any provision which treats a penalty under section 98A of that Act as if it were tax charged in an assessment and due and payable.
@ref sch 1 para 7(8) (src:4624)
GIVEN `a provision treats the penalty as if it were tax charged in an assessment and due and payable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 7(8) sub-paragraph (6) has effect` MEANS
    -- the answer is the same whether or not such a provision applies: "notwithstanding any provision"
    TRUE OR `a provision treats the penalty as if it were tax charged in an assessment and due and payable`

-- (9): "any reference to a year of assessment shall be construed, in relation to a contributions return, as a reference to the tax year corresponding to that year of assessment".
-- src:4625 | (9) In the application of section 98A of that Act by virtue of this paragraph, any reference to a year of assessment shall be construed, in relation to a contributions return, as a reference to the tax year corresponding to that year of assessment.
@ref sch 1 para 7(9) (src:4625)
GIVEN `the calendar year in which the year of assessment begins` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Tax year`
`sch 1 para 7(9) the tax year corresponding to the year of assessment` MEANS
    `Tax year` OF `the calendar year in which the year of assessment begins`

-- (10): in applying section 100D (court proceedings for penalties in cases of fraud): subsection (2) has effect with the omission of the words " or Northern Ireland " and paragraph (c);
-- subsection (3) with the omission of the words from " and any such proceedings instituted in Northern Ireland " onwards.
DECLARE `sch 1 para 7(10) subsection of section 100D` IS ONE OF
    `sch 1 para 7(10)(a) subsection (2)`
    `sch 1 para 7(10)(b) subsection (3)`
    `sch 1 para 7(10) some other subsection`

-- src:4626 | (10) In the application of section 100D of that Act (court proceedings for penalties in cases of fraud) by virtue of this paragraph—
-- src:4627 | (a) subsection (2) shall have effect with the omission of the words “ or Northern Ireland ” and paragraph (c); and
-- src:4628 | (b) subsection (3) shall have effect with the omission of the words from “ and any such proceedings instituted in Northern Ireland ” onwards.
@ref sch 1 para 7(10) (src:4626-4628)
GIVEN subsection IS A `sch 1 para 7(10) subsection of section 100D`
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`sch 1 para 7(10) what is omitted in applying the subsection` MEANS
    CONSIDER subsection
    WHEN `sch 1 para 7(10)(a) subsection (2)` THEN JUST "the words ' or Northern Ireland ' and paragraph (c)"
    WHEN `sch 1 para 7(10)(b) subsection (3)` THEN JUST "the words from ' and any such proceedings instituted in Northern Ireland ' onwards"
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the sub-paragraph modifies subsections (2) and (3) and says nothing of any other
    WHEN `sch 1 para 7(10) some other subsection` THEN NOTHING

-- (11)(a): in applying section 103 (time limit for recovery), a reference in subsection (1) to tax "shall be taken to include a reference to Class 1, Class 1A and Class 1B contributions".
-- src:4629 | (11) In the application of section 103 of that Act (time limit for recovery) by virtue of this paragraph—
-- src:4630 | (a) any reference in subsection (1) to tax shall be taken to include a reference to Class 1, Class 1A and Class 1B contributions;
@ref sch 1 para 7(11)(a) (src:4629-4630)
GIVEN class IS A `Class of contribution`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 7(11)(a) the reference to tax in section 103(1) includes the contributions` MEANS
    CONSIDER class
    WHEN `Class 1 primary` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Class 1 secondary` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Class 1A` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Class 1B` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "taken to include a reference to Class 1, Class 1A and Class 1B contributions" does not close the list
    WHEN `Class 2` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `Class 3` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `Class 3A` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `Class 4` THEN NOTHING

-- (11)(b): "any penalty by virtue of sub-paragraph (4) above shall be regarded as a penalty in respect of the tax return in question".
-- src:4629 | (11) In the application of section 103 of that Act (time limit for recovery) by virtue of this paragraph—
@ref sch 1 para 7(11)(b) (src:4629)
-- src:4631 | (b) any penalty by virtue of sub-paragraph (4) above shall be regarded as a penalty in respect of the tax return in question; and
@ref sch 1 para 7(11)(b) (src:4631)
GIVEN `the penalty is imposed by virtue of sub-paragraph (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 7(11)(b) the penalty is regarded as a penalty in respect of the tax return` MEANS
    IF `the penalty is imposed by virtue of sub-paragraph (4)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any penalty by virtue of sub-paragraph (4) above"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (11)(c): where, by virtue of subsection (2) (death), subsection (1)(b) does not apply to a penalty under section 98A(2)(b) or (4) in respect of a tax return, "it shall also not apply in relation to a penalty so imposed in respect of
-- the associated contributions return".
-- src:4629 | (11) In the application of section 103 of that Act (time limit for recovery) by virtue of this paragraph—
@ref sch 1 para 7(11)(c) (src:4629)
-- src:4632 | (c) where, by virtue of subsection (2) (death), subsection (1)(b) does not apply in relation to a penalty under section 98A(2)(b) or (4) of that Act in respect of a tax return, it shall also not apply in relation to a penalty so imposed in respect of the associated contributions return.
@ref sch 1 para 7(11)(c) (src:4632)
GIVEN `section 103(1)(b) does not apply to the penalty in respect of the tax return by virtue of subsection (2) (death)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 7(11)(c) section 103(1)(b) applies to the penalty in respect of the associated contributions return` MEANS
    IF `section 103(1)(b) does not apply to the penalty in respect of the tax return by virtue of subsection (2) (death)`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it shall also not apply in relation to a penalty so imposed in respect of the associated contributions return"
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "where, by virtue of subsection (2) (death), subsection (1)(b) does not apply"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (12): a penalty under section 98A "shall not be imposed where" (a) a decision relating to contributions falls to be made under section 8, 10 or 11 of the 1999 Act and has not yet been made, and (b) it will affect liability for the penalty or its amount.
-- src:4633 | (12) A penalty under section 98A of that Act as it applies by virtue of this paragraph shall not be imposed where—
-- src:4634 | (a) a decision relating to contributions falls to be made under or by virtue of section 8, 10 or 11 of the Social Security Contributions (Transfer of Functions, etc.) Act 1999, and has not yet been made; and
-- src:4635 | (b) the decision will affect a person’s liability for the penalty, or the amount of it.
@ref sch 1 para 7(12) (src:4633-4635)
GIVEN `a decision relating to contributions falls to be made under or by virtue of section 8, 10 or 11 of the Social Security Contributions (Transfer of Functions, etc.) Act 1999, and has not yet been made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision will affect a person's liability for the penalty, or the amount of it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 7(12) a penalty under section 98A may be imposed` MEANS
    IF `a decision relating to contributions falls to be made under or by virtue of section 8, 10 or 11 of the Social Security Contributions (Transfer of Functions, etc.) Act 1999, and has not yet been made`
       AND `the decision will affect a person's liability for the penalty, or the amount of it`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A penalty under section 98A of that Act as it applies by virtue of this paragraph shall not be imposed where"
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar is for the case (a) and (b) describe
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (13)(b): a contributions return and a tax return "are 'associated' if" the contributions return is required to be made (i) at the same time as the tax return, or (ii) where sub-paragraph (1)(b) applies, at a time defined by reference to the time for making the tax return.
-- (13)(a): "contributions return" and "tax return" are construed in accordance with sub-paragraph (1): the names of the facts above follow it.
-- src:4636 | (13) For the purposes of this paragraph—
-- src:4637 | (a) “contributions return” and “tax return” shall be construed in accordance with sub-paragraph (1) above; and
-- src:4638 | (b) a contributions return and a tax return are “associated” if the contributions return is required to be made—
-- src:4639 | (i) at the same time as the tax return, or
-- src:4640 | (ii) where sub-paragraph (1)(b) above applies, at a time defined by reference to the time for making the tax return.
@ref sch 1 para 7(13) (src:4636-4640)
GIVEN `the contributions return is required to be made at the same time as the tax return` IS A BOOLEAN
      `sub-paragraph (1)(b) applies and the contributions return is required to be made at a time defined by reference to the time for making the tax return` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 7(13) the contributions return and the tax return are associated` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a contributions return and a tax return are “associated” if" (i) or (ii) (a definition by "if")
    `the contributions return is required to be made at the same time as the tax return`
        OR `sub-paragraph (1)(b) applies and the contributions return is required to be made at a time defined by reference to the time for making the tax return`

§§ `Paragraph 7A -- penalties for fraud or negligence in contributions returns (label inferred)`

-- (1): "This paragraph applies where paragraph 7 above applies".
-- src:4641 | (1) This paragraph applies where paragraph 7 above applies; and in this paragraph “contributions return” has the same meaning as in that paragraph.
@ref sch 1 para 7A(1) (src:4641)
GIVEN `paragraph 7 applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 7A(1) this paragraph applies` MEANS
    IF `paragraph 7 applies` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This paragraph applies where paragraph 7 above applies"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- The day n years on, for "within six years after the date" and "within three years after": the anniversary. A 29 February has no anniversary in a year that is not a leap year, and the text does not say which day stands in.
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sch 1 paras 7A and 7B the year is a leap year` MEANS
    ((year MODULO 4 EQUALS 0) AND (NOT (year MODULO 100 EQUALS 0))) OR (year MODULO 400 EQUALS 0)

GIVEN years IS A NUMBER
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`sch 1 paras 7A and 7B the anniversary of the day` MEANS
    IF (DATE_DAY day EQUALS 29) AND (DATE_MONTH day EQUALS 2) AND (NOT `sch 1 paras 7A and 7B the year is a leap year` ((DATE_YEAR day) PLUS years))
    -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): a 29 February has no anniversary in a year that is not a leap year, and the text does not say which day stands in
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (Date (DATE_DAY day) (DATE_MONTH day) ((DATE_YEAR day) PLUS years))

-- (3)(b): regulations under sub-paragraph (2) shall "provide for the penalty to be imposed by the Inland Revenue within six years after the date on which the penalty is incurred".
-- src:4645 | (3) Regulations under sub-paragraph (2) above shall—
@ref sch 1 para 7A(3)(b) (src:4645)
-- src:4647 | (b) provide for the penalty to be imposed by the Inland Revenue within six years after the date on which the penalty is incurred;
@ref sch 1 para 7A(3)(b) (src:4647)
GIVEN `the day the penalty is incurred` IS A DATE
      `the day the penalty is imposed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 7A(3)(b) the penalty may be imposed by the Inland Revenue on the day` MEANS
    CONSIDER `sch 1 paras 7A and 7B the anniversary of the day` 6 `the day the penalty is incurred`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST lastDay THEN
        IF (`the day the penalty is incurred` LESS THAN `the day the penalty is imposed`)
           AND ((`the day the penalty is imposed` LESS THAN lastDay) OR (`the day the penalty is imposed` EQUALS lastDay))
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "within six years after the date on which the penalty is incurred"; outside that period the sub-paragraph grants nothing
        ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Paragraph 7B -- collection of contributions otherwise than through the PAYE system`

-- (3): as 6(4), for decisions under section 8, 9, 10, 12, 14 or 15 of the Social Security Act 1998 and interest under (2)(e).
-- src:4667 | (3) Where—
-- src:4668 | (a) a decision relating to contributions falls to be made under section 8, 9, 10, 12, 14 or 15 of the Social Security Act 1998; and
-- src:4669 | (b) the decision will affect a person’s liability for, or the amount of, any interest due in respect of those contributions,
-- src:4670 | regulations under sub-paragraph (2)(e) above shall not require any such interest to be paid until the decision has been made.
@ref sch 1 para 7B(3) (src:4667-4670)
GIVEN `a decision relating to contributions falls to be made under section 8, 9, 10, 12, 14 or 15 of the Social Security Act 1998` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision will affect a person's liability for, or the amount of, any interest due in respect of those contributions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision has been made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 7B(3) regulations under sub-paragraph (2)(e) may require the interest to be paid` MEANS
    IF `a decision relating to contributions falls to be made under section 8, 9, 10, 12, 14 or 15 of the Social Security Act 1998`
       AND `the decision will affect a person's liability for, or the amount of, any interest due in respect of those contributions`
       AND (NOT `the decision has been made`)
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "regulations under sub-paragraph (2)(e) above shall not require any such interest to be paid until the decision has been made"
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar lasts "until the decision has been made" and covers only the cases described; the sub-paragraph grants nothing
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (5)(b): regulations under (2)(h) shall provide for the penalty to be imposed by the Inland Revenue (i) within six years after the date on which it is incurred; or (ii) where its amount is to be ascertained by reference to the
-- amount of any contributions payable, at any later time within three years after the final determination of the amount of those contributions.
-- src:4672 | (5) Regulations under sub-paragraph (2)(h) above shall—
@ref sch 1 para 7B(5)(b) (src:4672)
-- src:4674 | (b) ... provide for the penalty to be imposed by the Inland Revenue—
-- src:4675 | (i) within six years after the date on which the penalty is incurred; or
-- src:4676 | (ii) where the amount of the penalty is to be ascertained by reference to the amount of any contributions payable, at any later time within three years after the final determination of the amount of those contributions;
@ref sch 1 para 7B(5)(b) (src:4674-4676)
GIVEN `the day the penalty is incurred` IS A DATE
      `the amount of the penalty is to be ascertained by reference to the amount of any contributions payable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the final determination of the amount of those contributions` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day the penalty is imposed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 7B(5)(b) the penalty may be imposed by the Inland Revenue on the day` MEANS
    IF `sch 1 para 7A(3)(b) the penalty may be imposed by the Inland Revenue on the day` `the day the penalty is incurred` `the day the penalty is imposed` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE
        IF `the amount of the penalty is to be ascertained by reference to the amount of any contributions payable`
        THEN
            CONSIDER `the day of the final determination of the amount of those contributions`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST determined THEN
                CONSIDER `sch 1 paras 7A and 7B the anniversary of the day` 3 determined
                WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
                WHEN JUST lastDay THEN
                    IF (`the day the penalty is incurred` LESS THAN `the day the penalty is imposed`)
                       AND ((`the day the penalty is imposed` LESS THAN lastDay) OR (`the day the penalty is imposed` EQUALS lastDay))
                    THEN JUST TRUE
                    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "within three years after the final determination of the amount of those contributions"
                    ELSE NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "within six years after the date on which the penalty is incurred"; limb (ii) is for a penalty whose amount is ascertained by reference to contributions
        ELSE NOTHING

-- (8): interest or penalties may be charged for a period before section 57 of the Social Security Act 1998 came into force "but only to the extent that interest or penalties would have been chargeable if the contributions in question
-- had been recoverable, in respect of that period, by virtue of regulations under paragraph 6 above".
-- src:4683 | (8) Interest or penalties may be charged by virtue of regulations under this paragraph in respect of a period before the coming into force of section 57 of the Social Security Act 1998 but only to the extent that interest or penalties would have been chargeable if the contributions in question had been recoverable, in respect of that period, by virtue of regulations under paragraph 6 above.
@ref sch 1 para 7B(8) (src:4683)
GIVEN `the interest or penalties charged under regulations under paragraph 7B for the earlier period` IS A NUMBER
      `the interest or penalties that would have been chargeable under regulations under paragraph 6 for that period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`sch 1 para 7B(8) the interest or penalties that may be charged for the earlier period` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but only to the extent that interest or penalties would have been chargeable"
    min `the interest or penalties charged under regulations under paragraph 7B for the earlier period`
        `the interest or penalties that would have been chargeable under regulations under paragraph 6 for that period`

DECLARE `sch 1 para 7B(9) kind of thing referred to` IS ONE OF
    `sch 1 para 7B(9)(e) interest payable in respect of contributions by virtue of regulations under paragraph (e) of sub-paragraph (2)`
    `sch 1 para 7B(9)(h) a penalty payable in respect of contributions by virtue of regulations under paragraph (h) of sub-paragraph (2)`
    `sch 1 para 7B(9) something else`

-- (9): "Any reference to contributions in sub-paragraph (1) above shall be construed as including a reference to any interest or penalty payable, in respect of contributions, by virtue of regulations under paragraph (e) or (h) of sub-paragraph (2) above."
-- src:4684 | (9) Any reference to contributions in sub-paragraph (1) above shall be construed as including a reference to any interest or penalty payable, in respect of contributions, by virtue of regulations under paragraph (e) or (h) of sub-paragraph (2) above.
@ref sch 1 para 7B(9) (src:4684)
GIVEN thing IS A `sch 1 para 7B(9) kind of thing referred to`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 7B(9) the reference to contributions in sub-paragraph (1) includes the thing` MEANS
    CONSIDER thing
    WHEN `sch 1 para 7B(9)(e) interest payable in respect of contributions by virtue of regulations under paragraph (e) of sub-paragraph (2)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 1 para 7B(9)(h) a penalty payable in respect of contributions by virtue of regulations under paragraph (h) of sub-paragraph (2)` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "construed as including" does not close the list
    WHEN `sch 1 para 7B(9) something else` THEN NOTHING

-- (10): "The rate of interest applicable for any purpose of this paragraph shall be the rate from time to time prescribed under section 178 of the Finance Act 1989 for the corresponding purpose of paragraph 6 above."
-- src:4685 | (10) The rate of interest applicable for any purpose of this paragraph shall be the rate from time to time prescribed under section 178 of the Finance Act 1989 for the corresponding purpose of paragraph 6 above.
@ref sch 1 para 7B(10) (src:4685)
GIVEN `the rate from time to time prescribed under section 178 of the Finance Act 1989 for the corresponding purpose of paragraph 6` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`sch 1 para 7B(10) the rate of interest` MEANS
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the prescribed rate is not in this text and is an input
    `the rate from time to time prescribed under section 178 of the Finance Act 1989 for the corresponding purpose of paragraph 6`

§§ `Paragraph 7C -- recovery of contributions in a similar manner to income tax (label inferred)`

DECLARE `sch 1 para 7C(3) kind of thing referred to` IS ONE OF
    `sch 1 para 7C(3)(e) interest payable in respect of contributions by virtue of regulations under paragraph (e) of paragraph 7B(2)`
    `sch 1 para 7C(3)(h) a penalty payable in respect of contributions by virtue of regulations under paragraph (h) of paragraph 7B(2)`
    `sch 1 para 7C(3) something else`

-- (3): "Any reference to contributions in this paragraph shall be construed as including a reference to any interest or penalty payable, in respect of contributions, by virtue of regulations under paragraph (e) or (h) of paragraph 7B(2)."
-- src:4688 | (3) Any reference to contributions in this paragraph shall be construed as including a reference to any interest or penalty payable, in respect of contributions, by virtue of regulations under paragraph (e) or (h) of paragraph 7B(2).
@ref sch 1 para 7C(3) (src:4688)
GIVEN thing IS A `sch 1 para 7C(3) kind of thing referred to`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 7C(3) the reference to contributions in this paragraph includes the thing` MEANS
    CONSIDER thing
    WHEN `sch 1 para 7C(3)(e) interest payable in respect of contributions by virtue of regulations under paragraph (e) of paragraph 7B(2)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 1 para 7C(3)(h) a penalty payable in respect of contributions by virtue of regulations under paragraph (h) of paragraph 7B(2)` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "construed as including" does not close the list
    WHEN `sch 1 para 7C(3) something else` THEN NOTHING

§§ `Paragraph 10 -- deduction of contributions from pension, etc. (label inferred)`

-- (1): where a person is in receipt of a pension or allowance payable by the Secretary of State by virtue of a prescribed enactment or instrument, the Secretary of State "may with the consent of that person pay any contributions
-- (other than Class 1 or Class 4 contributions) payable by him and deduct the amount so paid from the pension or allowance".
-- src:4742 | (1) Where a person is in receipt of a pension or allowance payable by the Secretary of State by virtue of any prescribed enactment or instrument, the Secretary of State may with the consent of that person pay any contributions (other than Class 1 or Class 4 contributions) payable by him and deduct the amount so paid from the pension or allowance.
@ref sch 1 para 10(1) (src:4742)
GIVEN class IS A `Class of contribution`
      `the person is in receipt of a pension or allowance payable by the Secretary of State by virtue of a prescribed enactment or instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person consents` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 10(1) the Secretary of State may pay the contributions and deduct the amount from the pension or allowance` MEANS
    IF `the person is in receipt of a pension or allowance payable by the Secretary of State by virtue of a prescribed enactment or instrument`
       AND `the person consents`
       AND (NOT (class EQUALS `Class 1 primary`))
       AND (NOT (class EQUALS `Class 1 secondary`))
       AND (NOT (class EQUALS `Class 4`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "with the consent of that person" and "(other than Class 1 or Class 4 contributions)"; outside those limits the sub-paragraph grants nothing
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:4742 | (1) Where a person is in receipt of a pension or allowance payable by the Secretary of State by virtue of any prescribed enactment or instrument, the Secretary of State may with the consent of that person pay any contributions (other than Class 1 or Class 4 contributions) payable by him and deduct the amount so paid from the pension or allowance.
@ref sch 1 para 10(1) (src:4742)
GIVEN permitted IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the pension or allowance payable` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount so paid` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`sch 1 para 10(1) the pension or allowance left after the deduction` MEANS
    IF permitted EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN
        IF `the amount so paid` AT MOST `the pension or allowance payable`
        THEN JUST (`the pension or allowance payable` MINUS `the amount so paid`)
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text does not say what happens when the amount paid exceeds the pension or allowance payable
        ELSE NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): no deduction is provided for unless the Secretary of State may pay under the sub-paragraph
    ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `sch 1 para 10(2) kind of instrument` IS ONE OF
    `sch 1 para 10(2) an Act`
    `sch 1 para 10(2) a Royal Warrant`
    `sch 1 para 10(2) an Order in Council`
    `sch 1 para 10(2) an order`
    `sch 1 para 10(2) a scheme`
    `sch 1 para 10(2) something else`

-- (2): sub-paragraph (1) "shall have effect notwithstanding anything in any Act, Royal Warrant, Order in Council, order or scheme".
-- src:4743 | (2) Sub-paragraph (1) above shall have effect notwithstanding anything in any Act, Royal Warrant, Order in Council, order or scheme.
@ref sch 1 para 10(2) (src:4743)
GIVEN instrument IS A `sch 1 para 10(2) kind of instrument`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 10(2) sub-paragraph (1) has effect despite the instrument` MEANS
    CONSIDER instrument
    WHEN `sch 1 para 10(2) an Act` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 1 para 10(2) a Royal Warrant` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 1 para 10(2) an Order in Council` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 1 para 10(2) an order` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 1 para 10(2) a scheme` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the sub-paragraph names five kinds of instrument and does not say that no other overrides it
    WHEN `sch 1 para 10(2) something else` THEN NOTHING

§§ `Paragraph 11 -- sickness payments counting as remuneration (label inferred)`

-- (2): where regulations under sub-paragraph (1) require a registered friendly society to amend its rules, "the amendments may, notwithstanding any provision of those rules, be made in accordance with the procedure prescribed by regulations
-- made by the Chief Registrar of Friendly Societies for the purposes of this paragraph".
-- src:4746 | (2) In any case where regulations made under sub-paragraph (1) above have the effect of requiring a registered friendly society (within the meaning of the Friendly Societies Act 1974) to make amendments to its rules, the amendments may, notwithstanding any provision of those rules, be made in accordance with the procedure prescribed by regulations made by the Chief Registrar of Friendly Societies for the purposes of this paragraph.
@ref sch 1 para 11(2) (src:4746)
GIVEN `regulations made under sub-paragraph (1) have the effect of requiring a registered friendly society to make amendments to its rules` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amendments are made in accordance with the procedure prescribed by regulations made by the Chief Registrar of Friendly Societies for the purposes of this paragraph` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 11(2) the amendments may be made notwithstanding the society's rules` MEANS
    IF `regulations made under sub-paragraph (1) have the effect of requiring a registered friendly society to make amendments to its rules`
       AND `the amendments are made in accordance with the procedure prescribed by regulations made by the Chief Registrar of Friendly Societies for the purposes of this paragraph`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In any case where regulations ... have the effect of requiring ..., the amendments may ... be made in accordance with the procedure prescribed"
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `The power of paragraph 10(1) as a regulative rule (twin of the decision function above)`

-- A permission with no deadline: the text gives none. See NOTES.md for why the asserted answer is carried by the decision function.
DECLARE `sch 1 para 10(1) party` IS ONE OF
    `sch 1 para 10(1) the Secretary of State`

DECLARE `sch 1 para 10(1) action` IS ONE OF
    `sch 1 para 10(1) pays the contributions and deducts the amount from the pension or allowance`

-- src:4742 | (1) Where a person is in receipt of a pension or allowance payable by the Secretary of State by virtue of any prescribed enactment or instrument, the Secretary of State may with the consent of that person pay any contributions (other than Class 1 or Class 4 contributions) payable by him and deduct the amount so paid from the pension or allowance.
@ref sch 1 para 10(1) (src:4742)
`sch 1 para 10(1) the Secretary of State's permission to pay and deduct` MEANS
    PARTY `sch 1 para 10(1) the Secretary of State`
    MAY `sch 1 para 10(1) pays the contributions and deducts the amount from the pension or allowance`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST FULFILLED
